<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Palitana State</h1><p class="st-meta">1194 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Palitana</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Gohil Rajput state in Saurashtra whose territory held Shatrunjaya, the hill of nearly a thousand Jain temples and one of Jainism's holiest sites.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Palitana was ruled by a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gohil">Gohil Rajputs</a>, the clan that also ruled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bhavnagar-state">Bhavnagar State</a>; the Gohils entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a> in the 13th century, and tradition gives Palitana's line an early date. Firm records are mainly from the 17th century onward.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The state's fame came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shatrunjaya">Shatrunjaya</a> hill, covered with Jain temples built over many centuries by merchant patrons. The Thakore levied payments on pilgrims, which led to long disputes with the Jain community's trust, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anandji-kalyanji-trust">Anandji Kalyanji</a>. British officials brokered a series of agreements in the 19th century fixing an annual sum paid by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jainism">Jains</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Palitana joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saurashtra-state">United State of Saurashtra</a> in 1948 and is now a town in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bhavnagar-state">Bhavnagar</a> district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shatrunjaya">Shatrunjaya</a> remains a major pilgrimage centre.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/palitana-state.jpg" alt="Palitana State" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: Dr. Andreas Birken at German Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SaurashtraKart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1194 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Palitana</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Jainism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Palitana</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1571&amp;focus=palitana-state" aria-label="Palitana State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6608 1382 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Palitana State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6928 1638L7364 1601M6928 1638L7364 1602M6928 1638L6896 1610"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M6896 1610h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6928 1638h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6928 1638h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Palitana. <a href="/atlas?year=1571&amp;focus=palitana-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
